56,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I lean toward Candidate A. It provides the shared accessibility that drives high satisfaction and, as a hall conversion, it avoids the hazardous material risks of the older blocks' partitions.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I support Candidate A. It addresses the critical shortage of general-purpose rooms and, as a conversion of an underused hall, it minimizes the risk of disrupting the timetable and incurring off-site rental costs.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A is the only rational choice. It avoids the weather risks of C, the mechanical budget blowouts of D, and the ""appeal"" trap of B. It is a predictable path to completion.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for A too! It doesn't need the expensive mechanical plant work that D does, and it avoids the AV kit costs of B that we have no reserve for. It's the safest budget!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Candidate D would actually solve the technicians' manual labor crisis, but given the budget and schedule warnings from the rest of you, it's a non-starter. A is the only option that doesn't invite a catastrophe. I vote A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It is rare to see such immediate consensus. Since Candidate A satisfies our need for shared utility, avoids structural hazards, and remains fiscally predictable, I see no reason to deviate.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I agree. The alignment between the booking data and the low-impact nature of the hall conversion makes Candidate A the most responsible choice for the university's current operational constraints.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. When the evidence points so clearly toward a single path of least resistance, it would be an exercise in madness to seek out a more perilous one. I am quite content with A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! It feels great to pick something that won't surprise us with hidden costs later. Candidate A is definitely the way to go!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"It is almost touching how quickly you all converged on the safest possible option. While we leave the technicians to their manual labor, at least we can sleep soundly knowing our budget is intact. I concur.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Since we have reached a complete consensus based on the data, I believe we have done our due diligence. Candidate A is the most stable and beneficial investment for the campus.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I concur. The data on room usage and the need to protect the timetable make Candidate A the only choice that balances student needs with operational reality.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I believe we have exhausted the logic of the situation. To argue for any other candidate would be to invite a calendar slip for the sake of a whim. I vote for A.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm totally on board! A is the most honest plan we've got, and it's the one that actually fits our wallet. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I've already given my vote, but for the sake of completeness: A. It's the path of least resistance, and in this institution, that's usually the only path that actually reaches the destination.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
71,3,3,pass,Shunichi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
72,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I vote for Candidate A. It is the most logical choice, ensuring broad utility for the students while respecting the physical and financial constraints of our campus.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Candidate A. It is the only option that solves our space deficit while protecting the timetable from the costly disruptions we have seen in the past.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I cast my vote for Candidate A. It is the only selection that respects the laws of time and budget, ensuring we actually finish before the next decade begins.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I vote for Candidate A! It's the only one that doesn't risk a budget disaster, and it's a project we can actually afford to finish. A is my final choice!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
